WEBVTT

00:00:04.299 --> 00:00:07.135
"Newt Scamander with fiancée
Leta Lestrange,

00:00:08.011 --> 00:00:10.513
"brother Theseus and unknown woman."

00:00:10.889 --> 00:00:13.266
No. So Theseus is marrying Leta, not me.

00:00:14.017 --> 00:00:15.226
Oh!

00:00:16.437 --> 00:00:18.730
Oh... Oh, dear.

00:00:20.107 --> 00:00:21.190
Well...

00:00:22.151 --> 00:00:24.527
See, Teen read that,

00:00:24.987 --> 00:00:26.654
and she started dating someone else.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.032
He's an Auror.
His name's Achilles Tolliver.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.534
JACOB: Tolliver. (LAUGHING)

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:34.787
(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:00:37.958 --> 00:00:38.958
QUEENIE: Anyway...

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:42.462
We are real excited to be here, Newt.
This is a...

00:00:42.713 --> 00:00:44.213
Well, it's a special trip for us.

00:00:45.174 --> 00:00:47.633
You see, Jacob and I,

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:50.136
we're getting married.

00:00:51.889 --> 00:00:54.891
- (LAUGHING)
- I'm marrying Jacob.

00:00:56.852 --> 00:00:58.686
Ah! (LAUGHING)

00:01:00.355 --> 00:01:01.898
JACOB: Oh. (SIGHS)

00:01:02.483 --> 00:01:04.734
<i>NEWT: You've enchanted him, haven't you?</i>

00:01:05.819 --> 00:01:08.029
What? (LAUGHS NERVOUSLY)

00:01:08.113 --> 00:01:11.616
- I have not.
- Will you stop reading my mind?

00:01:11.784 --> 00:01:13.993
<i>Queenie, you've brought him here</i>
<i>against his will.</i>

00:01:14.161 --> 00:01:17.455
Oh, that is an outrageous accusation.
Look at him.

00:01:17.623 --> 00:01:20.625
He's just happy. He's so happy.

00:01:21.168 --> 00:01:22.168
Then you won't mind if I, um...

00:01:24.671 --> 00:01:25.880
Please don't.

00:01:26.048 --> 00:01:27.673
NEWT: Queenie, you've got nothing
to fear if he wants to get married.

00:01:27.841 --> 00:01:30.760
We can just lift the enchantment,
and he can tell us himself.

00:01:41.522 --> 00:01:42.563
JACOB: What do you got there?

00:01:43.232 --> 00:01:44.357
What are you gonna do?

00:01:44.441 --> 00:01:46.234
What are you gonna do with that,
Mr. Scamander?

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:47.860
<i>Surgito.</i>

00:01:47.945 --> 00:01:49.070
(GROANING)

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.370
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

00:01:59.206 --> 00:02:00.915
Congratulations
on your engagement, Jacob.

00:02:01.083 --> 00:02:02.291
Wait, what?

00:02:06.463 --> 00:02:08.339
Oh, no. You didn't.

00:02:11.176 --> 00:02:12.385
Queenie!

00:02:12.553 --> 00:02:13.636
One second.

00:02:14.596 --> 00:02:16.055
Queenie!

00:02:16.139 --> 00:02:18.349
- (DOOR OPENS)
- It's very nice to see you.

00:02:18.517 --> 00:02:19.559
- (DOOR CLOSES)
- Where the hell am I right now?

00:02:19.726 --> 00:02:20.726
Uh, London.

00:02:20.853 --> 00:02:21.853
Oh!

00:02:22.396 --> 00:02:23.980
I always wanted to go here!

00:02:24.648 --> 00:02:25.648
Queenie!

00:02:26.149 --> 00:02:27.316
(DOOR OPENS)

00:02:27.943 --> 00:02:28.943
(DOOR CLOSES)

00:02:29.653 --> 00:02:31.153
JACOB: Oh, Queenie, honey.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:33.656
Well, I'm curious
when you were gonna wake me up.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:35.074
After we had five kids?

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.371
Why is it wrong to wanna marry you?

00:02:40.539 --> 00:02:42.748
- Okay.
- To wanna have a family?

00:02:43.917 --> 00:02:46.377
I just want what everyone else has,
that's all.

00:02:49.131 --> 00:02:50.381
Wait, wait.

00:02:50.549 --> 00:02:52.466
We've talked about this
like a million times.

00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:54.093
If we get married and they find out,

00:02:54.177 --> 00:02:55.636
they're gonna
throw you in jail, sweetheart.

00:02:55.804 --> 00:02:57.972
- I can't have that.
- (SIGHS HEAVILY)

00:02:58.307 --> 00:03:00.933
They don't like people like me
marrying people like you.

00:03:01.101 --> 00:03:04.395
I ain't a wizard. I'm just me.

00:03:04.563 --> 00:03:08.190
They're really progressive here,
and they'll let us get married properly.

00:03:08.358 --> 00:03:10.776
Sweetheart, you don't need
to enchant me.

00:03:11.653 --> 00:03:13.237
I'm already enchanted.

00:03:14.364 --> 00:03:16.198
I love you so much.

00:03:16.366 --> 00:03:17.909
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

00:03:19.077 --> 00:03:21.871
But I can't have you
risking everything like this, you know?

00:03:22.039 --> 00:03:24.123
You're not giving us
a choice, sweetheart.

00:03:26.501 --> 00:03:28.210
You're not giving me a choice.

00:03:28.921 --> 00:03:31.631
One of us had to be brave,
and you were being a coward.

00:03:34.176 --> 00:03:35.843
I was being a coward?

00:03:36.553 --> 00:03:38.220
If I'm a coward, you're... (MUTTERS)

00:03:40.432 --> 00:03:41.432
Crazy.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:44.185
I didn't say it.

00:03:44.353 --> 00:03:47.063
- You didn't have to.
- No, I didn't mean it, sweetheart.

00:03:48.398 --> 00:03:49.440
Yeah, you did.

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:53.611
- No.
- I'm gonna go see my sister.

00:03:54.446 --> 00:03:55.696
Fine. See your sister.

00:03:55.864 --> 00:03:57.782
- Fine.
- No, wait! Wait!

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.784
No! Queenie!

00:04:01.828 --> 00:04:03.412
I didn't mean it.

00:04:05.707 --> 00:04:07.541
I didn't say nothin'.

00:04:08.627 --> 00:04:09.835
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

00:04:21.014 --> 00:04:22.515
<i>Papyrus Reparo.</i>

00:04:31.942 --> 00:04:32.984
(TINA'S VOICE)

00:04:42.536 --> 00:04:43.953
(CREATURE BRAYING)

00:04:44.997 --> 00:04:46.330
Hey, Newt!

00:04:46.707 --> 00:04:49.625
NEWT: Down here, Jacob.
So I'll be with you in a second.

00:04:50.127 --> 00:04:51.210
(SQUAWKS)

00:04:53.964 --> 00:04:55.297
I got my own problems.

00:05:20.532 --> 00:05:22.283
Queenie left a postcard.

00:05:22.451 --> 00:05:24.201
Tina's in Paris looking for Credence.

00:05:24.369 --> 00:05:25.453
Genius.

00:05:25.871 --> 00:05:27.621
Queenie's gonna go straight for Tina.

00:05:27.789 --> 00:05:29.331
Okay, we're going to France, pal.

00:05:29.499 --> 00:05:31.500
- Oh, hold on. I'll get my jacket.
- I've got it.

00:05:33.795 --> 00:05:34.920
Oh.

00:05:40.343 --> 00:05:41.343
Beautiful.

